@baseUrl = http://localhost:8090

### 1. Synchronous CQRS: command updates write + read model in one transaction
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/orders?projectionMode=SYNCHRONOUS
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference": "ORD-CQRS-SYNC",
  "customerId": "C-42",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 100.00 },
    { "sku": "MOUSE", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 40.00 }
  ]
}

### Use returned orderId below.
@syncOrderId = 1

### Query reads the flattened read model, not the write aggregate.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/orders/{{syncOrderId}}

### State shows both models aligned.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/state/{{syncOrderId}}

### 2. Deferred projection: write commits before read model refresh.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/orders?projectionMode=DEFERRED
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference": "ORD-CQRS-DEFERRED",
  "customerId": "C-99",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "MONITOR", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 300.00 }
  ]
}

@deferredOrderId = 2

### State: write model exists, readModel is null, pendingProjectionRefreshes > 0.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/state/{{deferredOrderId}}

### Query fails because read model is intentionally stale/missing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/orders/{{deferredOrderId}}

### Projection worker catches up.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/projections/refresh-next

### Query now succeeds.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/orders/{{deferredOrderId}}

### 3. Make write model PAID but defer read model update.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/orders/{{deferredOrderId}}/pay?projectionMode=DEFERRED

### State shows writeStatus=PAID while readModel.status can still be NEW.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/state/{{deferredOrderId}}

### Catch up.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/projections/refresh-next

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cqrs/state/{{deferredOrderId}}
